{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Ms. ___. I’m Dr. ___. You were brought in because your blood sugar was over 500. How are you feeling right now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay, just tired. My foot’s been bothering me, and my sugars have been really hard to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. You’ve been on antibiotics for your foot infection—vancomycin and ceftazidime. We think the infection might be making your sugars worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this ulcer for so long. Is it getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s still concerning. You’re scheduled for a below-the-knee amputation next week to help control the infection. We discussed it with vascular surgery, and they’re still planning to go ahead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I’m nervous about the surgery. Will I be safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your heart and overall health. You’re at higher risk because of your heart and diabetes, but we’ll make sure you’re ready. You may need to see cardiology before the surgery for clearance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We considered changing them because of resistant bacteria we’ve seen in the past, but you’re not showing signs of being very sick. We briefly switched to cefepime, but we’re going back to your usual vancomycin and ceftazidime since you want to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to stay in the hospital longer. I can take them at dialysis, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. You’ll get vancomycin and ceftazidime after each dialysis session, just like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my blood sugar—what’s going on there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked for diabetic ketoacidosis, but your blood isn’t acidic, so it’s not DKA. The infection is likely spiking your sugars. We gave you insulin, and it’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using my sliding scale. Should I keep doing that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep your usual insulin—NPH in the morning and the sliding scale as needed. We’ll keep an eye on it while you’re here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ve also been feeling a bit short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray. There’s some fluid buildup in your lungs from heart failure. You’re scheduled for dialysis today to help remove extra fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forgot I had that today. Will it help me breathe better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, most patients feel better after dialysis. We’ll also keep you on your heart meds—lisinopril, carvedilol, and others."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my sodium was low last time. Is that still an issue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium was 132 when you came in, but it’s now 136—much better. Nephrology recommends you stay on a 1-liter fluid restriction daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. It’s hard not to drink more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-05-25 14:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. Just do your best. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You just finished dialysis. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit tired, but my breathing feels easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your blood pressure is better too—131/50. The fluid removal helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Any other test results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white blood cell count is normal, so no major infection right now. The urine test showed some bacteria, but it’s likely contamination. No treatment change needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had so many UTIs. I’m not surprised."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-05-25 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with your history of catheter use, you’re at high risk. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-05-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar this morning is 140—well controlled. How’s your foot?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-05-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still sore, but no new drainage or redness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-05-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The wound looks stable. We’re keeping the dressing clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-05-26 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about gabapentin? I’ve been taking it for nerve pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-05-26 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned you didn’t want to continue it. We’ve stopped it, and you can restart if needed later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-05-26 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m okay without it for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. We’re getting close to discharge. Your labs are stable—sodium 136, glucose 119, and hemoglobin improved to 11.1."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Am I going home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning. You’ll go home with services to help you until surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my surgery prep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve told vascular surgery you’re high risk. They recommend you see cardiology before the amputation for clearance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make that appointment. And I keep my fluid limit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 1 liter per day. Also, weigh yourself every morning. Call your doctor if you gain more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my meds stay the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mostly. You’ll keep all your usual meds except gabapentin, which we stopped. Insulin, antibiotics with dialysis, heart meds—all continue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-05-27 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re finalizing your discharge. You’re doing well—alert, breathing fine, sugars controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: follow up with your primary doctor, keep your clinic appointments, and good luck with surgery next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. The nurse will go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also send a note to your podiatrist and vascular surgeon to keep them updated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s helpful. I want everyone on the same page."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’re all working together for your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—call us if your foot gets red, warm, or starts draining, or if your sugars go over 300 consistently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And if I feel short of breath again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially if it’s worse than usual. That could mean fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well this admission. We’re confident you’ll do well at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and good luck next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need it!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve got a strong team behind you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-05-28 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up or hear how the surgery went."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-05-25 13:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-05-28 18:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, and a history of recurrent diabetic foot ulcers was admitted for hyperglycemia with blood glucose over 500. The elevated sugars were attributed to a worsening left calcaneal osteomyelitis. She was not in DKA, and her blood sugar responded well to insulin. She underwent hemodialysis for volume overload, which improved her respiratory status and heart failure symptoms. Her sodium, which was initially low, normalized with fluid restriction. Antibiotics were briefly adjusted but reverted to her home regimen of vancomycin and ceftazidime per her preference. She was deemed a high-risk candidate for her upcoming below-the-knee amputation and advised to seek cardiology clearance. She was discharged home with services, continuing her insulin, antibiotics with dialysis, and all other home medications except gabapentin, which was discontinued.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Chronic osteomyelitis, ankle and foot",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Ulcer of heel and midfoot",
      "Other bone involvement in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
